# Who must review what (Deliverable 5: who reviews clinical-adjacent prompts).
# Branch ruleset on main: require a pull request, 2 approvals, review from Code Owners, and the status
# checks lint-test, eval, mcp-health, build-deploy. GitHub needs only one owner per matching line,
# so the PR template's sign-off checklist asks for BOTH clinical_ops and ml-eng on clinical paths.
#
# The @afyaplus/* teams are the target org setup. In this single-author capstone repo they stand for
# roles the author played (see README, "Fallbacks declared").

*                               @afyaplus/ml-eng

# Clinical-adjacent: what the model is told, what "correct" means, and which answers were recorded.
/prompts/                       @afyaplus/clinical-ops @afyaplus/ml-eng
/evals/                         @afyaplus/clinical-ops @afyaplus/ml-eng
/fixtures/                      @afyaplus/clinical-ops @afyaplus/ml-eng
/triage_engine.py               @afyaplus/clinical-ops @afyaplus/ml-eng
/config/                        @afyaplus/ml-eng @afyaplus/clinical-ops
/clinical_ops_change_brief.md   @afyaplus/clinical-ops

# MCP tool contracts: agents in other services depend on these schemas.
/logistics_mcp_versioned.py     @afyaplus/ml-eng @afyaplus/platform
/mcp_schema.lock.json           @afyaplus/ml-eng @afyaplus/platform
/clinics.json                   @afyaplus/platform @afyaplus/clinical-ops

# The pipeline itself: changing a gate is a change to the rules.
/.github/                       @afyaplus/platform @afyaplus/ml-eng
/azure-pipelines.yml            @afyaplus/platform @afyaplus/ml-eng
/scripts/check_mcp_health.py    @afyaplus/platform @afyaplus/ml-eng
/eval_prompts.py                @afyaplus/ml-eng @afyaplus/clinical-ops
